# {{ app_name }} test harness

An LLM-driven harness for testing {{ app_name }} against BA-written test cases. Claude reads the English, picks test data,
and judges results. A small CLI does everything with side effects: allowlisted single-row inserts, updates and
deletes in the QA database, API calls from a fixed list of named operations, polling, snapshots of the evidence,
reverting all of it, and an Excel report BAs can open.

```text
workbook.xlsx ──test-compile──▶ specs/*.yaml ──test-run + CLI──▶ runs/<case>/<ts>/ ──report──▶ results.xlsx
               (Claude reads,    (reviewed by                  (manifest, responses,          (Results, Runs,
                queries, writes)  you and BAs)                  collect snapshots, verdict)    Changes sheets)
```

## Quick start

```bash
uv sync
cp .env.example .env
uv run python -m harness.stub --init-db demo.sqlite                  # terminal 1: the demo app
uv run --env-file .env harness --config demo/harness.toml run-case demo/specs/EXAMPLE-001.yaml --yes
uv run --env-file .env harness --config demo/harness.toml report --out results.xlsx --workbook demo/ba-test-cases.xlsx
```

For {{ app_name }}, open Claude Code here and ask it to set the harness up (the `harness-setup` skill).
`docs/setup.md` has the demo walkthrough, the manual setup steps, and what the CLI enforces.

## Layout

| Path | What | Owner |
|---|---|---|
| `harness/cli.py` | commands: `status`, `dump-workbook`, `validate`, `sql`, `run-case`, `revert`, `results`, `verdict`, `report` | template |
| `harness/run.py` | the case lifecycle and the manifest; revert lives in a `finally` | template |
| `harness/db.py` | sqlite, Oracle and MSSQL adapter, allowlisted writes, before-image ledger, revert, read-only query | template |
| `harness/api.py` | named operations: render, call, capture, poll | template |
| `harness/spec.py`, `harness/config.py` | spec and `harness.toml` models and checks | template |
| `harness/results.py`, `harness/report.py` | duckdb over the evidence; workbook dump and Excel report | template |
| `harness/stub.py`, `demo/` | a demo pricing app with its config, specs and BA workbook | template |
| `.claude/skills/` | `harness-setup`, `test-compile`, `test-run` | template |
| `harness.toml`, `.env` | this app's QA targets, allowlist, operations, secrets | app |
| `specs/` | this app's compiled test cases, one YAML per case | app |
| `docs/glossary.md`, `schema.md`, `api.md`, `outputs.md` | this app's vocabulary, tables, API and evidence | app |

Template-owned files come from the template and are replaced by `uvx copier update`; change them in the template.

## Safety properties, enforced in the CLI

- Refuses a DSN or base URL that does not look like QA (`qa_markers`).
- DB writes touch only allowlisted tables, ops and columns, one row each, by full key. API calls are named operations only; setup operations must have an undo.
- Every undo record is on disk before the change it undoes. The revert always runs, in reverse order.
- A failed revert or a killed run leaves `runs/PENDING_REVERT`. Every command then prints a banner and `run-case` refuses to start. The marker is also the run lock: one case at a time.
- Mutating commands show their plan and do nothing without `--yes`.
